Error classification
--------------------

Parse and decode failures thrown by GifReader (and its frame decode methods)
are GifError instances (a subclass of Error) carrying two extra fields:

  - category: one of the GifErrorCategory strings
      'bad_header'             not a GIF 87a/89a signature
      'truncated'              the stream ended before the current structure
                               (the message names the decoder state machine
                               state in which the data ran out)
      'lzw_overflow'           the LZW stream decodes to more pixels than the
                               frame holds
      'unsupported_extension'  an unknown extension label was encountered
      'malformed'              a structurally invalid block (bad sizes,
                               markers, LZW min code size, etc)
  - offset: the byte offset into the input buffer where the problem was
    detected.

See test/error_classification.js for a malformed-sample acceptance matrix
(run it with: node test/error_classification.js).
